---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import verified from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-12/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-12/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/14-12/',prod='https://www.espec.co.jp/english/products/env-test/sh/',spec='https://espec.com/images/uploads/files/t_su-sh_benchtop.pdf',reg='https://www.espec.co.th/th/product/env-test/sh';
const fields=[['initialC','Initial package (°C)',-60,150,20],['stepC','Air step setpoint (°C)',-60,150,40],['rhPercent','RH setpoint (%)',0,100,65],['tauS','Package time constant (s)',10,3600,120],['holdS','Hold (s)',10,14400,480]];
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+Number(v.toPrecision(9))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="ESPEC SH-262 environmental chamber" subtitle="" description="Measure the ideal thermal response of an inert package after an air temperature step." wide={true}>
<article id="env" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/14-12/">← Equipment 14-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#env-proof">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">14-12 / Environmental test / Inert thermal phantom</p><h2>ESPEC SH-262</h2><p>Run a virtual 20 → 40 °C step and see the package reach 32.64 °C after one 120 s time constant. Open the cabinet to inspect the shelf, or try a setpoint above 75 °C to see the virtual humidity profile reject it.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Open the cabinet</h3><div class="e-row" id="env-views">{['Bench','Front','Rack','Side','Rear'].map(k=><button data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="env-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="env-model" aria-label="Orbitable ESPEC SH-262 cabinet with interactive door"></canvas><p id="env-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Click or tap the solid door, inert package or controller. Drag to orbit; pinch or scroll to zoom. The form has the same actions for keyboard use.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Run a step and hold</h3><form id="env-form">
<div class="e-row"><button type="button" id="env-door">Open door</button><button type="button" id="env-load">Remove phantom</button></div>
<div class="e-fields"><label>Package ID<input name="sampleId" value="inert-package-01" maxlength="96" required/></label>
{fields.map(([k,t,l,h,v])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min={l} max={h} step="any" value={v}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="env-run" class="e-run" type="submit">Run profile</button><button id="env-reset" type="button">Restore example</button></div>
</form><p id="env-status" role="status">Door closed. Phantom present.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Review the trace</h3><p id="env-result" role="status">No profile run.</p><svg id="env-plot" viewBox="0 0 550 190" role="img" aria-label="Chamber target and simulated phantom temperature over time"></svg><p>Dashed line: imposed air setpoint. Blue: sample temperature. Marker: one time constant, if the hold lasts that long.</p><div class="e-row"><button id="env-json" disabled>Trace JSON</button><button id="env-csv" disabled>Trace CSV</button></div></section>
<section><h3>Selected configuration</h3><p>22.5 L SH-262 with solid door and wire rack. Nominal W/H/D 440 × 690 × 786 mm and cavity W/H/D 300 × 300 × 250 mm. The <a href={reg}>regional ESPEC dimensions table</a> and <a href={spec}>manufacturer outline drawing</a> differ by about 1 mm in depth. The actual controller, vent/port shapes and rack details are simplified. Compare <a href={prod}>ESPEC product photography and humidity performance plot</a>. These drawings are original geometry projections, not manufacturer photos.</p>
<div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original solid-door ESPEC model"/></figure><figure><img src={a+'work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original ESPEC open rack and inert specimen"/></figure></div></section>
<section><h3>What the simulation computes</h3><p>The air setpoint is an <strong>ideal instantaneous step</strong>, not the achievable chamber ramp. A lumped inert package follows T(t) = Tₐ + (T₀ − Tₐ) exp(−t/τ). τ can represent thermal capacitance divided by heat-transfer conductance. The model logs a target RH but does not solve moisture uptake, condensation, chamber airflow or compressor behavior. The teaching humidity profile is restricted to 20–75 °C and 60–85% RH at assumed conditioned ambient, a conservative subwindow rather than the manufacturer's full operating envelope. Out-of-profile inputs produce a code and no trace.</p>
<p>JSON and CSV retain sample ID, elapsed seconds, °C, programmed RH, provenance and revisions. <a href={a+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a> · <a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example export</a>. This is not chamber certification.</p></section>
<section id="env-proof"><h3>Analytic verification and assets</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody>{verified.map(v=><tr><td>{v.id}</td><td>{show(v.expected)}</td><td>{show(v.actual)}</td><td>{v.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases/tolerances</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Evidence</a> · <a href={a+'espec-sh-262.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable source</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>XR anchors</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} material primitives. Optional WebXR; physical headset untested.</p></section></article>
</Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/14-12/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#env header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#env h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#env section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#env button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#env button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#env-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#env-plot{width:100%;max-height:13rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#env table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#env td,#env th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#env figure{margin:0}#env img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
